id: E778
draft: true
contributor_id: 2501
trigger_tool: patch-ng|conan|patch
phase: source-patching
error_signature: hunk no.1 doesn't match source file|expected:.*actual:.*indent
severity: 2
category: patch-delivery, conan, portability
match_keywords: GNU patch fuzz, patch_ng exact context, indentation mismatch, conandata patch, source byte identity
title: GNU patch dry-run success does not prove Conan patch-ng can apply a whitespace-drifted hunk
root_cause: GNU patch can accept a hunk with fuzz by dropping mismatched context, whereas Conan patch-ng validates the context bytes at the target location. A one-space indentation error in an unchanged context line can therefore pass a local dry-run but fail the actual Conan build before configure. A release configure shebang and inherited CONFIG_SHELL can select different interpreters. A mksh-only print choice then damages generated Libtool when config.status is run by Bash. Explicitly invoke the declared Bash configure interpreter and keep that interpreter bound in CONFIG_SHELL/SHELL.
affected_scope: Conan recipes delivering unified diffs for Autotools scripts or other whitespace-sensitive source files when local validation uses GNU patch and target Conan uses patch-ng.
verification_cmd: Run patch_ng.fromfile(...).apply(strip=1, root=<fresh source copy>, fuzz=False); execute the patched script's target tuple probe; then confirm a fresh Conan create proceeds beyond apply_conandata_patches.
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: byte-exact-conan-patch-preflight
rec_description: Compare every context line with the source bytes including indentation, validate with the same patch-ng engine and zero fuzz used by Conan, then run the changed script and a fresh target Conan create. A release configure shebang and inherited CONFIG_SHELL can select different interpreters. A mksh-only print choice then damages generated Libtool when config.status is run by Bash. Explicitly invoke the declared Bash configure interpreter and keep that interpreter bound in CONFIG_SHELL/SHELL.
rec_command: Use a fresh task-private source copy for patch_ng fuzz=False, then run sh config.sub aarch64-unknown-linux-ohos and the current Conan recipe.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: patch-context-repair
forbid_1_pattern: GNU patch.*fuzz.*PASS.*therefore.*Conan
forbid_1_reason: GNU fuzz may discard the mismatched context line that patch-ng requires exactly.
forbid_1_consequence: Conan fails during apply_conandata_patches before configure despite a green local dry-run.
principles: []
causes: []
caused_by: []
similar_to: [E279, DRAFT-conan-patch-hunk-exact-line-offset]
conflicts_with: []
prerequisite_of: []
