last_updated: 2026-10-13
source_event: libdvbcsa 1.1.0 historical patch-ng mismatch; CI80106 config.status Permission denied; libdvbcsa-w3-20261010T095900Z Conan RC0 upstream4/4 consumer1/1 log SHA256 b3372b7bd5f0bccb6250718b28ed02df25bb271ff721cee2474a9c98d205f8d2 2026-10-13 current CI repair; libdvbcsa-ci-repair-w3-20261013-r2, official CI log SHA256 6ad4f9d309cf6b6ef588e78753d71760bfe3dbff1e0034e0ae12bbfa838dea64; This adds the first-causal-generation-error boundary to existing temporary-directory knowledge: configure RC0 and a later make error are not proof of valid generated scripts. A signed .libs ELF still does not authorize its unsigned shell launcher: explicitly interpret the four unchanged Libtool launchers with the declared Bash TESTS_ENVIRONMENT, preserving their environment setup and exit status. The first consumed run stalled at binaryload_event_call and remains FAIL; its exact owned children were cleaned only with explicit user authorization. Reuse the existing HMDFS execution mechanism, not a new signing invention; do not edit libtool or skip any test.
ci_increment: Exact patch acceptance does not prove generated configure directory permissions. On mapped-identity HMDFS mktemp -d forces0700 even with a permissive outer umask. Match both release creation branches strictly and use task-local exclusive mkdir under umask007 with existing cleanup, not postcreation chmod or global directories.
